---
import { models } from './figures.mjs';
interface Props { kind: keyof typeof models; number: number; }
const {kind,number}=Astro.props;
const m=models[kind];
const id=`pa-${kind}`;
const staticLookup = kind === "lookup";
---
<figure class="pa-figure" data-pa-player={staticLookup ? undefined : kind} aria-labelledby={`${id}-title`}>
 <figcaption id={`${id}-title`}><span class="pa-number">Figure {number}</span> <strong>{m.title}</strong></figcaption>
 <div class="pa-drawing" data-pa-scene data-live set:html={m.frame(staticLookup ? 4 : 0)}></div>
 {!staticLookup && <><p class="pa-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">{m.steps[0]}</p>
 <div class="pa-controls">
  {m.choices.length>0 && <label>Compare <select data-pa-choice aria-label={`Comparison for figure ${number}`}>{m.choices.map(([value,label])=><option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></label>}
  <div class="pa-buttons" role="group" aria-label={`Playback for figure ${number}`}>
   <button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / {m.steps.length}</span>
  </div>
  <div data-hold class="pa-hold" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 </div>
 </>}
 <p class="pa-caption">{m.caption}</p>
 <details class="pa-text"><summary>Figure as text</summary>{m.choices.length>0&&<p>With only the primary-key index and same-page space, P7 keeps its index entry to (12,3); that tuple links to the heap-only version at (12,4). After retention ends, item 3 can redirect to item 4. A price B-tree instead requires new price and primary-key entries for (12,4). With no room on page 12, the new tuple goes to (13,1) and needs a new primary-key entry. The non-HOT versions require coordinated heap and index cleanup. These are independent replays.</p>}<ol>{m.steps.map(text=><li>{text}</li>)}</ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
 import {models} from './figures.mjs';
 for (const root of document.querySelectorAll('[data-pa-player]')) {
  const kind=root.getAttribute('data-pa-player');
  const m=models[kind];
  const choice=root.querySelector('select');
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>m.steps.length,draw:(s)=>{
   root.querySelector('[data-pa-scene]').innerHTML=m.frame(s,choice?.value);
   root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=m.steps[s];
  }});
  choice?.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
 }
</script>
